            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "NFL kicks off big season for sports bets. Fanatics exec weighs in.",
            "description": "<p>The 2025 NFL season officially kicks off Thursday night with the Dallas Cowboys paired up to play the Philadelphia Eagles. This presents a fresh opportunity for sports betting companies to gain some yardage this quarter.</p>\n<p>Fanatics Betting and Gaming CEO Matt King speaks with Asking for a Trend's <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> to speak on his platform's sports betting features and what sports betting competitors can anticipate in the coming football months.</p>\n<p>Catch Yahoo Finance's <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/draftkings-ceo-q2-sports-betting-173000677.html\">full interview </a>with DraftKings (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DKNG\">DKNG</a>) CEO Jason Robins from August.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination/\">Market Domination</a>.</p>",
